					<div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2175">Ferriciean Aetas</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2176">Dolere Necare</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2177">Sedyei</a></div><div class="xsmall"><a href="http://www.guildsay.com/guilds/view_character.php?id=2178">Relegare</a></div>					
					<br>
				</td>
				<td width="70%" class="body" valign="top">
					<table width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0">
					<tr>
						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Myrjala/Vyia has just brought an excellent idea to my attn.  We should have a guild bank.  In this bank we would store items that we do not wish/Can't sell or wish for other members of the guild to be able to use.  Such as a really nice weapon that you have, but you also have better... put it in the bank.  We could keep up with the acct items on the guild page i'm going to write.  these items would in no way be OWNED by anyone who wanted them; they would belong to the guild, or whomever put them into the bank if they wished to retain ownership (if they wish to retain ownership they MUST indicate that when they put it in, otherwise the item becomes no ones).  when you &quot;check out&quot; an item you may keep it as long as you need it, but must return it when you upgrade, and these items are NOT for sale, unless agreed upon by all the officers, and the person who deposited it in the first place.  if sold, the money would go to the appropriate place (if the depositor wishes to retain ownership, he/she would get the money, otherwise it would go into the guild acct).  whatya think guys?  there of course will have to be some more thinking on this; and of course we will have to decide who creates the acct's to store the stuff on (i propose faythea because i think everyone trusts her - but it's up to her AND up to whether or not she has the space hehe).  Let me know!  And everyone who has yet to email NobleAlliance@yahoo.com AND register on guildsay.com, please do so so that we may know who all's here!<br />
<br />
Ferriciean Aetas<br />
Bard Advisor						</td>
